<title>JAPAN: Showa Yokkaichi delays restart of 90,000bpd topper.</title>
<headline>Showa Yokkaichi delays restart of 90,000bpd topper.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Showa Yokkaichi Sekiyu Co Ltd said on Tuesday that it would restart its 90,000 barrel-per-day crude distillation unit at Yokkaichi, central Japan, on Wednesday, one day later than originally scheduled.</p>
<p>The topper has been shut since October 6 for routine maintenance operations, and a delay in the work held up the restart, a refinery official said.</p>
<p>Showa Yokkaichi Sekiyu is a refinery in the Showa Shell Sekiyu KK group. Showa Shell is owned 50 percent by the Royal Dutch/Shell Group.</p>
</text>
